  "raw": " China. The earliest Hui influence was introduced in highly significant periods of the city's history, including: the Wars of the Five Dynasties, the Themes Seal of the Five Dynasties Period, the Three Kingdoms Period, the Susaki Period, and the Tang Dynasty Period. During the foreign conquest and invasion period, Queen Hui, the wife of Sima Yi (the ruler of Susang) (in the late 7th century CE), reconciled with Liu Zhao, the ruler of the Deng Zhou (a very powerful state that bordered the Yi kingdom) in the early 11th century CE. Wedding ceremony in Nurhing (a neolithic facility), Puyuma (in the city of Nanjing), c. 950 AD.Photograph by Yuhua Zhang, Nanjing Public Museum.",
  "serialized": "China. The earliest Hui influence was introduced in highly significant periods of the city's history, including: the Wars of the Five Dynasties, the Themes Seal of the Five Dynasties Period, the Three Kingdoms Period, the Susaki Period, and the Tang Dynasty Period. During the foreign conquest and invasion period, Queen Hui, the wife of Sima Yi (the ruler of Susang) (in the late 7th century CE), reconciled with Liu Zhao, the ruler of the Deng Zhou (a very powerful state that bordered the Yi kingdom) in the early 11th century CE. Wedding ceremony in Nurhing (a neolithic facility), Puyuma (in the city of Nanjing), c. 950 AD.Photograph by Yuhua Zhang, Nanjing Public Museum.",
